{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "1CH",
  "chapter": 17,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "1CH.17.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CH.17.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Now it came to pass, as David sat in his house, that David said to Nathan the prophet, Lo, I dwell in a house of cedars, but the ark of the covenant of the LORD ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "remaineth",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " under curtains.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "1CH.17.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CH.17.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then Nathan said to David, Do all that ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in thy heart; for God ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " with thee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CH.17.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CH.17.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And it came to pass the same night, that the word of God came to Nathan, saying,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CH.17.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CH.17.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Go and tell David my servant, Thus saith the LORD, Thou shalt not build me a house to dwell in:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CH.17.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CH.17.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For I have not dwelt in a house since the day that I brought up Israel to this day; but have gone from tent to tent, and from ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "one",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " tabernacle ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "to another",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CH.17.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CH.17.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Wherever I have walked with all Israel, have I spoken a word to any of the judges of Israel, whom I commanded to feed my people, saying, Why have ye not built me a house of cedars?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CH.17.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CH.17.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Now therefore thus shalt thou say to my servant David, Thus saith the LORD of hosts, I took thee from the sheep-cote, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "even",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " from following the sheep, that thou shouldst be ruler over my people Israel:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CH.17.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CH.17.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And I have been with thee whithersoever thou hast walked, and have cut off all thy enemies from before thee, and have made thee a name like the name of the great men that ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in the earth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CH.17.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CH.17.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Also I will ordain a place for my people Israel, and will plant them, and they shall dwell in their place, and shall be moved no more; neither shall the children of wickedness waste them any more, as at the beginning.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CH.17.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CH.17.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And since the time that I commanded judges ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "to be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " over my people Israel. Moreover, I will subdue all thy enemies. Furthermore, I tell thee that the LORD will build thee a house.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CH.17.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CH.17.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And it shall come to pass, when thy days shall be ended that thou must go ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "to be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " with thy fathers, that I will raise up thy seed after thee, who shall be of thy sons; and I will establish his kingdom.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CH.17.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CH.17.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He shall build me a house, and I will establish his throne for ever.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CH.17.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CH.17.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I will be his father, and he shall be my son: and I will not take my mercy away from him, as I took ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " from ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "him",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " that was before thee:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CH.17.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CH.17.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But I will settle him in my house and in my kingdom for ever: and his throne shall be established for evermore.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CH.17.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CH.17.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "According to all these words, and according to all this vision, so did Nathan speak to David.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CH.17.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CH.17.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And David the king came and sat before the LORD, and said, Who ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "am",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " I, O LORD God, and what ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " my house, that thou hast brought me hitherto?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CH.17.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CH.17.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "yet",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " this was a small thing in thy eyes, O God; for thou hast ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "also",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " spoken of thy servant's house for a great while to come, and hast regarded me according to the estate of a man of high degree, O LORD God.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CH.17.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CH.17.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "What can David ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "speak",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " more to thee for the honor of thy servant? for thou knowest thy servant.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CH.17.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CH.17.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "O LORD, for thy servant's sake, and according to thy own heart, hast thou done all this greatness, in making known all ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "these",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " great things.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CH.17.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CH.17.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "O LORD, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " is none like thee, neither ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is there any",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " God besides thee, according to all that we have heard with our ears.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CH.17.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CH.17.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And what one nation in the earth ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " like thy people Israel, whom God went to redeem ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "to be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " his own people, to make thee a name of greatness and terribleness, by driving out nations from before thy people, whom thou hast redeemed out of Egypt?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CH.17.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CH.17.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For thy people Israel didst thou make thy own people for ever; and thou, LORD, becamest their God.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CH.17.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CH.17.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Therefore now, LORD, Let the thing that thou hast spoken concerning thy servant and concerning his house be established for ever, and do as thou hast said.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CH.17.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CH.17.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let it even be established, that thy name may be magnified for ever, saying, The LORD of hosts ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the God of Israel, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "even",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a God to Israel: and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "let",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the house of David thy servant ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " established before thee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CH.17.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CH.17.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For thou, O my God, hast told thy servant that thou wilt build him a house: therefore thy servant hath found ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "in his heart",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to pray before thee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CH.17.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CH.17.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And now, LORD, thou art God, and hast promised this goodness to thy servant:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CH.17.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CH.17.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Now therefore let it please thee to bless the house of thy servant, that it may be before thee for ever: for thou blessest, O LORD, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it shall be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " blessed for ever.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
